      {
        "bounds": [
          28.0,
          168.0,
          580.0,
          49.0
        ],
        "name": "Today we are splitting Ghostty's core into a library. The app you run keeps its window, its fonts and its configuration; the terminal underneath becomes something another program can embed.",
        "role": "label"
      },
      {
        "bounds": [
          28.0,
          231.0,
          580.0,
          49.0
        ],
        "name": "The surface is deliberately small. A host hands libghostty a native surface and a size, and gets back a grid of cells it can draw however it likes. Input arrives as an event queue, not as callbacks into the host's event loop.",
        "role": "label"
      },
      {
        "bounds": [
          40.0,
